1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,292
Let’s list the virtual machines on a Linux KVM host, then open its audit log.

2
00:00:06,292 --> 00:00:10,417
We’ll check whether the client had to request a log entry.

3
00:00:10,417 --> 00:00:14,375
Ask your AI to list the virtual machines.

4
00:00:14,375 --> 00:00:19,083
For this test, the client called the list tool directly.

5
00:00:19,083 --> 00:00:25,292
It then requested the status of an invalid test ID so we could see what a failure looks like.

6
00:00:25,292 --> 00:00:29,625
Open a terminal as the user running the KVM server.

7
00:00:29,625 --> 00:00:35,750
Its default work directory is dot vamp slash remote, under your home directory.

8
00:00:35,750 --> 00:00:40,333
If you set a custom work directory, open that instead.

9
00:00:40,333 --> 00:00:43,708
Use tail to read the last two lines.

10
00:00:43,708 --> 00:00:48,125
The first line shows the list tool returned a response.

11
00:00:48,125 --> 00:00:52,250
The second shows the status request ended in an error.

12
00:00:52,250 --> 00:00:56,958
Each line contains a time, a tool name and an outcome.

13
00:00:56,958 --> 00:01:00,875
The invalid input value appears in neither line.

14
00:01:00,875 --> 00:01:04,000
The file mode was six hundred.

15
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:07,542
It grants read and write access to the owner.

16
00:01:07,542 --> 00:01:11,500
A returned response tells you about the tool call.

17
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:18,000
To confirm an action succeeded inside a guest application, check the workflow’s own result.

18
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:22,750
Some Vault delivery paths record when a credential is resolved.

19
00:01:22,750 --> 00:01:29,083
Delivery happens afterwards, so this event alone cannot confirm a successful login.

20
00:01:29,083 --> 00:01:34,583
To check a volume mount, inspect the mount list in the relevant environment.

21
00:01:34,583 --> 00:01:41,083
In the CLI development build, select a workflow in the library and open Run history.

22
00:01:41,083 --> 00:01:46,833
The order exports passed their CSV checks on all three tested hypervisors.

23
00:01:46,833 --> 00:01:50,958
The unified audit screen is still a design proposal.
